IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21, Chapter 1 -- Certification and transfer of
-- securities: general (ss 768 to 782; lines 9962-10105 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively, written
-- from the text alone; it takes nobody's point of view. The seat layer is coa17-seat.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Every quote line
-- below is copied from that rendering by build script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110: no section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no YMD (dates are `Date day month year`).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; the rulings of 2026-11-04 and
-- 2026-11-05 and the case-by-case instruction of 2026-11-05 govern what they cover).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a condition introduced by "if", "only if",
--               "unless", "while", "until", "except", a flat negative ("does not", "may not", "is not required"), a
--               period or a "where"/"when" condition the text fixes in its own words. Every such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: silent, list not closed, "includes", undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording ("without", "as the transferee may reasonably request", a named
--               complement). Every such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Where a section combines two answers, the helpers of coa17-helpers.l4
--   do it (JUST FALSE settles a conjunction, JUST TRUE a disjunction, otherwise NOTHING stays NOTHING).
--
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 4): "officer in default" is asked as an INPUT named for the answering section, `s 1121 the
-- officer is in default` (MAYBE BOOLEAN), by every offence rule here.
--
-- DATES. "within two months after" counts the corresponding day two months later (clamped to the last day of a shorter
-- month); "within ten days after service" is the tenth day after. The Act states no month-counting rule (fork F2).
-- Today's date is never read: a question that depends on "now" takes `the day on which the question is asked` as input.

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F2 at s 769(1), s 771(1), s 776(1); F3 at s 779(1); F5 at s 771(1); F6
-- at s 781(1), s 781(2); F10 at s 768(2), s 770(1), s 771(1A); F11 at s 781(2); F16 at s 779(1); F17 at s 779(3); F18
-- at s 782(1).

§ `Part 21 Chapter 1: Certification and transfer of securities: general`

§§ `Share certificates (s 768)`

-- src:9965 | 768 Share certificate to be evidence of title
-- src:9966 | (1) In the case of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, a certificate under the common seal of the company specifying any shares held by a member is prima facie evidence of his title to the shares.
@ref s 768(1) Share certificate to be evidence of title (src:9965-9966)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies shares held by a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 768(1) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the member's title to the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
    WHEN Scotland THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` AND `the certificate specifies shares held by a member`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate under the common seal of the company specifying any shares held by a member is prima facie evidence"

-- src:9967 | (2) In the case of a company registered in Scotland—
-- src:9968 | (a) a certificate under the common seal of the company specifying any shares held by a member, or
-- src:9969 | (b) a certificate specifying any shares held by a member and subscribed by the company in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 7),
-- src:9970 | is sufficient evidence, unless the contrary is shown, of his title to the shares.
@ref s 768(2) Share certificate to be evidence of title (Scotland) (src:9967-9970)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is subscribed by the company in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies shares held by a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 768(2) the certificate is sufficient evidence of the member's title to the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
    WHEN Scotland THEN
        IF (   `the certificate is under the common seal of the company`
            OR `the certificate is subscribed by the company in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`)
           AND `the certificate specifies shares held by a member`
        THEN IF `the contrary is shown`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficient evidence, unless the contrary is shown"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate specifying any shares held by a member"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company registered in Scotland"

§§ `Issue of certificates etc on allotment (s 769)`

-- src:9973 | (1) A company must, within two months after the allotment of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:9974 | (a) the certificates of the shares allotted,
-- src:9975 | (b) the debentures allotted, or
-- src:9976 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock allotted.
@ref s 769(1) Duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on allotment (src:9973-9976)
DECLARE `s 769(1) what was allotted` IS ONE OF
    `s 769(1) shares allotted`
    `s 769(1) debentures allotted`
    `s 769(1) debenture stock allotted`

DECLARE `s 769(1) the documents to be completed and ready for delivery` IS ONE OF
    `s 769(1)(a) the certificates of the shares allotted`
    `s 769(1)(b) the debentures allotted`
    `s 769(1)(c) the certificates of the debenture stock allotted`

-- src:9977 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:9978 | (a) if the conditions of issue of the shares, debentures or debenture stock provide otherwise,
-- src:9979 | (b) in the case of allotment to a financial institution (see section 778), or
-- src:9980 | (c) in the case of an allotment of shares if, following the allotment, the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779).
@ref s 769(2) Subsection (1) does not apply (src:9977-9980)
DECLARE `s 769 allotment` HAS
    `s 769(1) the thing allotted` IS A `s 769(1) what was allotted`
    `s 769(1) the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
    `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9973 | (1) A company must, within two months after the allotment of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:9974 | (a) the certificates of the shares allotted,
-- src:9975 | (b) the debentures allotted, or
-- src:9976 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock allotted.
@ref s 769(1) the documents the company must complete and have ready (src:9973-9976)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
GIVETH A `s 769(1) the documents to be completed and ready for delivery`
`s 769(1) the documents the company must complete and have ready for delivery` MEANS
    CONSIDER allotment's `s 769(1) the thing allotted`
    WHEN `s 769(1) shares allotted` THEN `s 769(1)(a) the certificates of the shares allotted`
    WHEN `s 769(1) debentures allotted` THEN `s 769(1)(b) the debentures allotted`
    WHEN `s 769(1) debenture stock allotted` THEN `s 769(1)(c) the certificates of the debenture stock allotted`

-- src:9977 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:9978 | (a) if the conditions of issue of the shares, debentures or debenture stock provide otherwise,
-- src:9979 | (b) in the case of allotment to a financial institution (see section 778), or
-- src:9980 | (c) in the case of an allotment of shares if, following the allotment, the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779).
@ref s 769(2) Subsection (1) does not apply (src:9977-9980)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769(2) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF    allotment's `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise`
       OR allotment's `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution`
       OR (    allotment's `s 769(1) the thing allotted` EQUALS `s 769(1) shares allotted`
           AND allotment's `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Subsection (1) does not apply— (a) if ..., (b) in the case of ..., (c) in the case of ..." names the cases where it does not apply and does not say "only"

-- src:9973 | (1) A company must, within two months after the allotment of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock, complete and have ready for delivery—
@ref s 769(1) the company must, within two months after the allotment, complete and have ready for delivery (src:9973)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 769(2) subsection (1) does not apply` allotment
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 769(1) within two months after the allotment (src:9973)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 769(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` MEANS
    `s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` (allotment's `s 769(1) the day of the allotment`)

-- src:9981 | (3) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 769(3) default is made in complying with subsection (1) (src:9981)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
      `the day on which the documents were complete and ready for delivery` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769(3) default is made in complying with subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 769(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` allotment
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the day on which the documents were complete and ready for delivery`
        WHEN JUST done THEN
            IF done GREATER THAN `s 769(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` allotment
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within two months after the allotment"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 769(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` allotment
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within two months after the allotment" (the period has not yet ended)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) is not decided

@ref s 769(3) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default (src:9981)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769(3) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:9982 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 769(4) liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 and a daily default fine (src:9982)
`s 769(4) the penalty` MEANS
    `s 769(4) the penalty on summary conviction of a fine at a level and a daily default fine` 3 0.1

§§ `Transfer of securities (ss 770 to 775)`

-- src:9985 | (1) A company may not register a transfer of shares in or debentures of the company unless—
-- src:9986 | (a) a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to it, or
-- src:9987 | (b) the transfer—
-- src:9988 | (i) is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982 (c. 41), or
-- src:9989 | (ii) is in accordance with regulations under Chapter 2 of this Part.
@ref s 770(1) Registration of transfer (src:9985-9989)
GIVEN `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is in accordance with regulations under Chapter 2 of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(1) the bar on registering the transfer applies` MEANS
    IF    `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company`
       OR `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
       OR `the transfer is in accordance with regulations under Chapter 2 of this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not register a transfer of shares in or debentures of the company unless—" (the unless is met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9990 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect any power of the company to register as shareholder or debenture holder a person to whom the right to any shares in or debentures of the company has been transmitted by operation of law.
@ref s 770(2) a person to whom the right has been transmitted by operation of law (src:9990)
GIVEN `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(2) subsection (1) does not affect the company's power to register the person` MEANS
    IF `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to register as shareholder or debenture holder a person to whom the right to any shares in or debentures of the company has been transmitted by operation of law"

-- src:10005 | (5) This section does not apply—
-- src:10006 | (a) in relation to a transfer of shares if the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779);
-- src:10007 | (b) in relation to the transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law.
@ref s 771(5) This section does not apply (src:10005-10007)
DECLARE `s 771 lodged transfer` HAS
    `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS A DATE
    `s 771(5)(a) the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 771(5)(b) the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 771(1) what the company did with the lodged transfer` IS ONE OF
    `s 771(1)(a) registered the transfer`
    `s 771(1)(b) gave the transferee notice of refusal with its reasons`
    `s 771(1) did neither`

@ref s 771(5) This section does not apply (src:10005-10007)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 771 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(5) this section does not apply` MEANS
    IF    transfer's `s 771(5)(a) the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`
       OR transfer's `s 771(5)(b) the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section does not apply— (a) ..., (b) ..." names the cases where it does not apply and does not say "only"

-- src:9993 | (1) When a transfer of shares in or debentures of a company has been lodged with the company, the company must either—
-- src:9994 | (a) register the transfer, or
-- src:9995 | (b) give the transferee notice of refusal to register the transfer, together with its reasons for the refusal,
-- src:9996 | as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date on which the transfer is lodged with it.
@ref s 771(1) Procedure on transfer being lodged (src:9993-9996)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 771 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(1) the company must register the transfer or give the transferee notice of refusal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 771(5) this section does not apply` transfer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 771(1) within two months after the date on which the transfer is lodged (src:9993-9996)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 771 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 771(1) the last day for registering the transfer or giving notice of refusal` MEANS
    `s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` (transfer's `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged`)

@ref s 771(1) as soon as practicable and in any event within two months (src:9993-9996)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 771 lodged transfer`
      `what the company did` IS A `s 771(1) what the company did with the lodged transfer`
      `the day on which it did so` IS A DATE
      `it did so as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(1) the company has complied with subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 771(1) the company must register the transfer or give the transferee notice of refusal` transfer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply", so there is no subsection (1) duty to have complied with
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `what the company did`
        WHEN `s 771(1) did neither` THEN
            IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 771(1) the last day for registering the transfer or giving notice of refusal` transfer
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must either (a) register the transfer, or (b) give the transferee notice of refusal to register the transfer, together with its reasons" (a bare must not done: fork F5)
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether a company that has not yet acted within the two months has complied
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the day on which it did so` GREATER THAN `s 771(1) the last day for registering the transfer or giving notice of refusal` transfer
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event within two months after the date on which the transfer is lodged with it"
            ELSE IF `it did so as soon as practicable`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable"

-- src:9997 | (1A) The company may not register the transfer under subsection (1)(a) unless satisfied that it has the information that it is required to enter in its register of members in relation to the transferee.
@ref s 771(1A) The company may not register the transfer unless satisfied (src:9997)
GIVEN `the company is satisfied that it has the information that it is required to enter in its register of members in relation to the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(1A) the bar on registering the transfer under subsection (1)(a) applies` MEANS
    IF `the company is satisfied that it has the information that it is required to enter in its register of members in relation to the transferee`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not register the transfer under subsection (1)(a) unless satisfied" (the unless is met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9998 | (2) If the company refuses to register the transfer, it must provide the transferee with such further information about the reasons for the refusal as the transferee may reasonably request.
-- src:9999 | This does not include copies of minutes of meetings of directors.
@ref s 771(2) further information about the reasons for the refusal (src:9998-9999)
GIVEN `the company refuses to register the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee may reasonably request the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information requested is copies of minutes of meetings of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(2) the company must provide the transferee with the further information requested` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company refuses to register the transfer`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company refuses to register the transfer"
    ELSE IF `the information requested is copies of minutes of meetings of directors`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not include copies of minutes of meetings of directors."
         ELSE IF `the transferee may reasonably request the information`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such further information about the reasons for the refusal as the transferee may reasonably request"

-- src:10001 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10002 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10003 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 771(3)(a) an offence is committed by the company (src:10001-10003)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(3)(a) an offence is committed by the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company fails to comply with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section" (the if fails)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company failed is not decided

@ref s 771(3)(b) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default (src:10001-10003)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(3)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the company fails to comply with this section` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10004 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 771(4) liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 and a daily default fine (src:10004)
`s 771(4) the penalty` MEANS
    `s 769(4) the penalty on summary conviction of a fine at a level and a daily default fine` 3 0.1

-- src:10008 | 772 Transfer of shares on application of transferor
-- src:10009 | On the application of the transferor of any share or interest in a company, the company shall enter in its register of members the name of the transferee ... in the same manner and subject to the same conditions as if the application for the entry ... were made by the transferee.
@ref s 772 Transfer of shares on application of transferor (src:10008-10009)
GIVEN `the transferor of a share or interest in the company has applied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions on which the company would enter the transferee's name on the transferee's own application are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 772 the company must enter the name of the transferee in its register of members` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transferor of a share or interest in the company has applied to the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the application of the transferor of any share or interest in a company" (the "on ... application" condition fails)
    ELSE IF `the conditions on which the company would enter the transferee's name on the transferee's own application are met`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the same manner and subject to the same conditions as if the application for the entry ... were made by the transferee"

-- src:10010 | 773 Execution of share transfer by personal representative
-- src:10011 | An instrument of transfer of the share or other interest of a deceased member of a company—
-- src:10012 | (a) may be made by his personal representative although the personal representative is not himself a member of the company, and
-- src:10013 | (b) is as effective as if the personal representative had been such a member at the time of the execution of the instrument.
@ref s 773 Execution of share transfer by personal representative (src:10010-10013)
GIVEN `the instrument of transfer is of the share or other interest of a deceased member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument of transfer is made by the personal representative of the deceased member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 773(a) the personal representative may make the instrument of transfer although not a member` MEANS
    IF `the instrument of transfer is of the share or other interest of a deceased member of the company` AND `the instrument of transfer is made by the personal representative of the deceased member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An instrument of transfer of the share or other interest of a deceased member of a company"

@ref s 773(b) as effective as if the personal representative had been such a member (src:10010-10013)
GIVEN `the instrument of transfer is of the share or other interest of a deceased member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument of transfer is made by the personal representative of the deceased member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 773(b) the instrument is as effective as if the personal representative had been a member at the time of execution` MEANS
    IF `the instrument of transfer is of the share or other interest of a deceased member of the company` AND `the instrument of transfer is made by the personal representative of the deceased member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An instrument of transfer of the share or other interest of a deceased member of a company"

-- src:10014 | 774 Evidence of grant of probate etc
-- src:10015 | The production to a company of any document that is by law sufficient evidence of the grant of—
-- src:10016 | (a) probate of the will of a deceased person,
-- src:10017 | (b) letters of administration of the estate of a deceased person, or
-- src:10018 | (c) confirmation as executor of a deceased person,
-- src:10019 | shall be accepted by the company as sufficient evidence of the grant.
@ref s 774 Evidence of grant of probate etc (src:10014-10019)
DECLARE `s 774 grant` IS ONE OF
    `s 774(a) probate of the will of a deceased person`
    `s 774(b) letters of administration of the estate of a deceased person`
    `s 774(c) confirmation as executor of a deceased person`
    `s 774 some other grant`

@ref s 774 shall be accepted by the company as sufficient evidence of the grant (src:10014-10019)
GIVEN `the grant the document evidences` IS A `s 774 grant`
      `the document is by law sufficient evidence of the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 774 the company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document is by law sufficient evidence of the grant`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document that is by law sufficient evidence of the grant"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the grant the document evidences`
         WHEN `s 774 some other grant` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) probate of the will of a deceased person, (b) letters of administration of the estate of a deceased person, or (c) confirmation as executor of a deceased person"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:10025 | (a) an instrument of transfer is certificated if it bears the words “certificate lodged” (or words to the like effect);
@ref s 775(4)(a) an instrument of transfer is certificated (src:10025)
GIVEN `the instrument bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(4)(a) the instrument of transfer is certificated` MEANS
    IF `the instrument bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an instrument of transfer is certificated if it bears the words “certificate lodged” (or words to the like effect)"

-- src:10029 | (c) a certification is treated as signed by a person if—
-- src:10030 | (i) it purports to be authenticated by his signature or initials (whether handwritten or not), and
-- src:10031 | (ii) it is not shown that the signature or initials was or were placed there neither by himself nor by a person authorised to use the signature or initials for the purpose of certificating transfers on the company's behalf.
@ref s 775(4)(c) a certification is treated as signed by a person (src:10029-10031)
GIVEN `the certification purports to be authenticated by the person's signature or initials` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the signature or initials was or were placed there neither by the person nor by a person authorised to use them for the purpose of certificating transfers on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(4)(c) the certification is treated as signed by the person` MEANS
    IF `the certification purports to be authenticated by the person's signature or initials`
       AND (NOT `it is shown that the signature or initials was or were placed there neither by the person nor by a person authorised to use them for the purpose of certificating transfers on the company's behalf`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a certification is treated as signed by a person if (i) it purports to be authenticated by his signature or initials ... and (ii) it is not shown that ..."

-- src:10026 | (b) the certification of an instrument of transfer is made by a company if—
-- src:10027 | (i) the person issuing the instrument is a person authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf, and
-- src:10028 | (ii) the certification is signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf or by an officer or employee either of the company or of a body corporate so authorised;
@ref s 775(4)(b) the certification of an instrument of transfer is made by a company (src:10026-10028)
GIVEN `the person issuing the instrument is authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification is signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification is signed by an officer or employee either of the company or of a body corporate so authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(4)(b) the certification of the instrument of transfer is made by the company` MEANS
    IF    `the person issuing the instrument is authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf`
       AND (   `the certification is signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf`
            OR `the certification is signed by an officer or employee either of the company or of a body corporate so authorised`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the certification of an instrument of transfer is made by a company if (i) ... and (ii) ..."

-- src:10021 | (1) The certification by a company of an instrument of transfer of any shares in, or debentures of, the company is to be taken as a representation by the company to any person acting on the faith of the certification that there have been produced to the company such documents as on their face show a prima facie title to the shares or debentures in the transferor named in the instrument.
@ref s 775(1) Certification of instrument of transfer: a representation by the company (src:10021)
GIVEN `the certification is made by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted on the faith of the certification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(1) the certification is taken as a representation that documents showing a prima facie title in the transferor have been produced` MEANS
    IF `the certification is made by the company` AND `the person acted on the faith of the certification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a company of an instrument of transfer ... to any person acting on the faith of the certification"

-- src:10022 | (2) The certification is not to be taken as a representation that the transferor has any title to the shares or debentures.
@ref s 775(2) The certification is not to be taken as a representation that the transferor has any title (src:10022)
GIVEN `the certification is made by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(2) the certification is taken as a representation that the transferor has any title to the shares or debentures` MEANS
    IF `the certification is made by the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certification is not to be taken as a representation that the transferor has any title to the shares or debentures."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) speaks only of "The certification" in subsection (1)

-- src:10023 | (3) Where a person acts on the faith of a false certification by a company made negligently, the company is under the same liability to him as if the certification had been made fraudulently.
@ref s 775(3) A false certification made negligently (src:10023)
GIVEN `a person acts on the faith of a false certification by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification was made negligently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775(3) the company is under the same liability to the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently` MEANS
    IF `a person acts on the faith of a false certification by the company` AND `the certification was made negligently`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person acts on the faith of a false certification by a company made negligently" (the where condition fails)

§§ `Issue of certificates etc on transfer (ss 776 and 777)`

-- src:10034 | (1) A company must, within two months after the date on which a transfer of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock is lodged with the company, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:10035 | (a) the certificates of the shares transferred,
-- src:10036 | (b) the debentures transferred, or
-- src:10037 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock transferred.
@ref s 776(1) Duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer (src:10034-10037)
DECLARE `s 776(1) what was transferred` IS ONE OF
    `s 776(1) shares transferred`
    `s 776(1) debentures transferred`
    `s 776(1) debenture stock transferred`

DECLARE `s 776(1) the documents to be completed and ready for delivery` IS ONE OF
    `s 776(1)(a) the certificates of the shares transferred`
    `s 776(1)(b) the debentures transferred`
    `s 776(1)(c) the certificates of the debenture stock transferred`

-- src:10038 | (2) For this purpose a “transfer” means—
-- src:10039 | (a) a transfer duly stamped and otherwise valid, or
-- src:10040 | (b) an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982 (c. 41),
-- src:10041 | but does not include a transfer that the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register.
-- src:10042 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:10043 | (a) if the conditions of issue of the shares, debentures or debenture stock provide otherwise,
-- src:10044 | (b) in the case of a transfer to a financial institution (see section 778), or
-- src:10045 | (c) in the case of a transfer of shares if, following the transfer, the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779).
-- src:10046 | (4) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 777 (cases where the Stock Transfer Act 1982 applies).
-- src:10047 | (5) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:10048 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:10049 | 777 Issue of certificates etc: cases within the Stock Transfer Act 1982
-- src:10050 | (1) Section 776(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer) does not apply in the case of a transfer to a person where, by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982, he is not entitled to a certificate or other document of or evidencing title in respect of the securities transferred.
-- src:10051 | (2) But if in such a case the transferee—
-- src:10052 | (a) subsequently becomes entitled to such a certificate or other document by virtue of any provision of those regulations, and
-- src:10053 | (b) gives notice in writing of that fact to the company,
-- src:10054 | section 776 (duty to company as to issue of certificates etc) has effect as if the reference in subsection (1) of that section to the date of the lodging of the transfer were a reference to the date of the notice.
@ref ss 776(2), 776(3) and 777 the facts about a lodged transfer (src:10038-10054)
DECLARE `s 776 lodged transfer` HAS
    `s 776(1) the thing transferred` IS A `s 776(1) what was transferred`
    `s 776(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS A DATE
    `s 776(2)(a) the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 776(2)(b) the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 776(2) the company is entitled to refuse to register the transfer and does not register it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 776(3)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 776(3)(b) the transfer is to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 776(3)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 777(2)(a) the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate by virtue of a provision of those regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 777(2)(b) the day on which the transferee gave the company notice in writing of that fact` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:10034 | (1) A company must, within two months after the date on which a transfer of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock is lodged with the company, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:10035 | (a) the certificates of the shares transferred,
-- src:10036 | (b) the debentures transferred, or
-- src:10037 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock transferred.
@ref s 776(1) the documents the company must complete and have ready (src:10034-10037)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A `s 776(1) the documents to be completed and ready for delivery`
`s 776(1) the documents the company must complete and have ready for delivery` MEANS
    CONSIDER transfer's `s 776(1) the thing transferred`
    WHEN `s 776(1) shares transferred` THEN `s 776(1)(a) the certificates of the shares transferred`
    WHEN `s 776(1) debentures transferred` THEN `s 776(1)(b) the debentures transferred`
    WHEN `s 776(1) debenture stock transferred` THEN `s 776(1)(c) the certificates of the debenture stock transferred`

-- src:10038 | (2) For this purpose a “transfer” means—
-- src:10039 | (a) a transfer duly stamped and otherwise valid, or
-- src:10040 | (b) an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982 (c. 41),
-- src:10041 | but does not include a transfer that the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register.
@ref s 776(2) "transfer" means (src:10038-10041)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776(2) the instrument is a transfer for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF    (   transfer's `s 776(2)(a) the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid`
           OR transfer's `s 776(2)(b) the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982`)
       AND (NOT transfer's `s 776(2) the company is entitled to refuse to register the transfer and does not register it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For this purpose a “transfer” means— (a) ... or (b) ... but does not include a transfer that the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register."

-- src:10042 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:10043 | (a) if the conditions of issue of the shares, debentures or debenture stock provide otherwise,
-- src:10044 | (b) in the case of a transfer to a financial institution (see section 778), or
-- src:10045 | (c) in the case of a transfer of shares if, following the transfer, the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779).
@ref s 776(3) Subsection (1) does not apply (src:10042-10045)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776(3) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF    transfer's `s 776(3)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise`
       OR transfer's `s 776(3)(b) the transfer is to a financial institution`
       OR (    transfer's `s 776(1) the thing transferred` EQUALS `s 776(1) shares transferred`
           AND transfer's `s 776(3)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares transferred`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Subsection (1) does not apply— (a) if ..., (b) in the case of ..., (c) in the case of ..." names the cases where it does not apply and does not say "only"

-- src:10050 | (1) Section 776(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer) does not apply in the case of a transfer to a person where, by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982, he is not entitled to a certificate or other document of or evidencing title in respect of the securities transferred.
@ref s 777(1) Section 776(1) does not apply to a transfer to a person not entitled to a certificate (src:10050)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(1) section 776(1) does not apply to the transfer` MEANS
    IF transfer's `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a transfer to a person where, by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982, he is not entitled to a certificate"

-- src:10051 | (2) But if in such a case the transferee—
-- src:10052 | (a) subsequently becomes entitled to such a certificate or other document by virtue of any provision of those regulations, and
-- src:10053 | (b) gives notice in writing of that fact to the company,
-- src:10054 | section 776 (duty to company as to issue of certificates etc) has effect as if the reference in subsection (1) of that section to the date of the lodging of the transfer were a reference to the date of the notice.
@ref s 777(2) the date of the notice is the date of the lodging of the transfer (src:10051-10054)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 777(2) the day treated as the day on which the transfer was lodged` MEANS
    CONSIDER transfer's `s 777(2)(b) the day on which the transferee gave the company notice in writing of that fact`
    WHEN JUST noticeDay THEN
        IF transfer's `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
           AND transfer's `s 777(2)(a) the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate by virtue of a provision of those regulations`
        THEN JUST noticeDay
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "But if in such a case the transferee— (a) subsequently becomes entitled ... and (b) gives notice in writing of that fact to the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the transferee has not given notice in writing

-- src:10050 | (1) Section 776(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer) does not apply in the case of a transfer to a person where, by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982, he is not entitled to a certificate or other document of or evidencing title in respect of the securities transferred.
-- src:10051 | (2) But if in such a case the transferee—
-- src:10052 | (a) subsequently becomes entitled to such a certificate or other document by virtue of any provision of those regulations, and
-- src:10053 | (b) gives notice in writing of that fact to the company,
-- src:10054 | section 776 (duty to company as to issue of certificates etc) has effect as if the reference in subsection (1) of that section to the date of the lodging of the transfer were a reference to the date of the notice.
@ref s 777(1) and (2) section 776(1) does not apply until the notice is given (src:10050-10054)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 777(1) section 776(1) does not apply to the transfer until notice is given` MEANS
    IF transfer's `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 777(2) the day treated as the day on which the transfer was lodged` transfer
         WHEN JUST noticeDay THEN FALSE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE

-- src:10046 | (4) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 777 (cases where the Stock Transfer Act 1982 applies).
@ref s 776(4) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 777 (src:10046)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 776(4) the day from which the period of two months runs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 777(2) the day treated as the day on which the transfer was lodged` transfer
    WHEN JUST noticeDay THEN noticeDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN transfer's `s 776(1) the day the transfer was lodged`

-- src:10034 | (1) A company must, within two months after the date on which a transfer of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock is lodged with the company, complete and have ready for delivery—
@ref s 776(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents (src:10034)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 776(2) the instrument is a transfer for the purposes of subsection (1)` transfer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For this purpose a “transfer” means"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 776(3) subsection (1) does not apply` transfer
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply"
        OTHERWISE
            IF `s 777(1) section 776(1) does not apply to the transfer until notice is given` transfer
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 776(1) ... does not apply in the case of a transfer to a person where ... he is not entitled to a certificate"
            ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 776(1) within two months after the date on which a transfer is lodged (src:10034)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 776(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` MEANS
    `s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` (`s 776(4) the day from which the period of two months runs` transfer)

-- src:10047 | (5) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 776(5) default is made in complying with subsection (1) (src:10047)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
      `the day on which the documents were complete and ready for delivery` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776(5) default is made in complying with subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 776(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` transfer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the day on which the documents were complete and ready for delivery`
        WHEN JUST done THEN
            IF done GREATER THAN `s 776(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` transfer
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within two months after the date on which a transfer ... is lodged with the company"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 776(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` transfer
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within two months after the date on which a transfer ... is lodged with the company" (the period has not yet ended)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) is not decided

@ref s 776(5) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default (src:10047)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776(5) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10048 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 776(6) liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 and a daily default fine (src:10048)
`s 776(6) the penalty` MEANS
    `s 769(4) the penalty on summary conviction of a fine at a level and a daily default fine` 3 0.1

§§ `Issue of certificates etc on allotment or transfer to financial institution (s 778)`

-- src:10057 | (1) A company—
-- src:10058 | (a) of which shares or debentures are allotted to a financial institution,
-- src:10059 | (b) of which debenture stock is allotted to a financial institution, or
-- src:10060 | (c) with which a transfer for transferring shares, debentures or debenture stock to a financial institution is lodged,
-- src:10061 | is not required in consequence of that allotment or transfer to comply with section 769(1) or 776(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc).
@ref s 778(1) Issue of certificates etc: allotment or transfer to financial institution (src:10057-10061)
GIVEN `shares or debentures of the company are allotted to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `debenture stock of the company is allotted to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer for transferring shares, debentures or debenture stock to a financial institution is lodged with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 778(1) the company is not required in consequence of the allotment or transfer to comply with section 769(1) or 776(1)` MEANS
    IF    `shares or debentures of the company are allotted to a financial institution`
       OR `debenture stock of the company is allotted to a financial institution`
       OR `a transfer for transferring shares, debentures or debenture stock to a financial institution is lodged with the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company— (a) of which shares or debentures are allotted to a financial institution, (b) ..., or (c) with which a transfer ... to a financial institution is lodged"

-- src:10062 | (2) A “financial institution” means—
-- src:10063 | (a) a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange, or
-- src:10064 | (b) a nominee of—
-- src:10065 | (i) a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in that way, or
-- src:10066 | (ii) a recognised investment exchange,
-- src:10067 | designated for the purposes of this section in the rules of the recognised investment exchange in question.
-- src:10068 | (3) Expressions used in subsection (2) have the same meaning as in Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8).
@ref s 778(2) "financial institution" means (borrowed terms: Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, s 778(3)) (src:10062-10068)
GIVEN `the person is a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a nominee of a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in that way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a nominee of a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is designated for the purposes of this section in the rules of the recognised investment exchange in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 778(2) the person is a financial institution` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange`
       OR (    (   `the person is a nominee of a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD acting in that way`
                OR `the person is a nominee of a recognised investment exchange`)
           AND `the person is designated for the purposes of this section in the rules of the recognised investment exchange in question`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “financial institution” means—"

§§ `Share warrants (ss 779 to 781)`

-- src:10071 | (1) A company limited by shares may, if so authorised by its articles, issue with respect to any fully paid shares a warrant (a “share warrant”) stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in it.
@ref s 779(1) A company limited by shares may, if so authorised by its articles, issue a share warrant (src:10071)
GIVEN `the liability of the members` IS A `Liability of members`
      `the articles authorise the company to issue share warrants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is with respect to fully paid shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(1) the company may issue a share warrant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the liability of the members`
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` THEN
        IF (NOT `the articles authorise the company to issue share warrants`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if so authorised by its articles" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F16: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
        ELSE IF `the warrant is with respect to fully paid shares`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to any fully paid shares"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company limited by shares"

@ref s 779(1) a warrant (a "share warrant") stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in it (src:10071)
GIVEN `the warrant states that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(1) the warrant is a share warrant` MEANS
    IF `the warrant states that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the parenthesis names the term "share warrant" and does not say "means" (fork F3)

-- src:10072 | (2) A share warrant issued under the company's common seal or (in the case of a company registered in Scotland) subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 7) entitles the bearer to the shares specified in it and the shares may be transferred by delivery of the warrant.
@ref s 779(2) A share warrant issued under the common seal entitles the bearer (src:10072)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the share warrant is issued under the company's common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(2) the share warrant entitles the bearer to the shares specified in it` MEANS
    IF    `the share warrant is issued under the company's common seal`
       OR (`the place where the company is registered` EQUALS Scotland AND `the share warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A share warrant issued under the company's common seal or (in the case of a company registered in Scotland) subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995"

@ref s 779(2) the shares may be transferred by delivery of the warrant (src:10072)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the share warrant is issued under the company's common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(2) the shares may be transferred by delivery of the warrant` MEANS
    `s 779(2) the share warrant entitles the bearer to the shares specified in it` `the place where the company is registered` `the share warrant is issued under the company's common seal` `the share warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`

-- src:10073 | (3) A company that issues a share warrant may, if so authorised by its articles, provide (by coupons or otherwise) for the payment of the future dividends on the shares included in the warrant.
@ref s 779(3) future dividends on the shares included in the warrant (src:10073)
GIVEN `the company issues a share warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles authorise the company to provide for the payment of the future dividends on the shares included in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(3) the company may provide for the payment of the future dividends on the shares included in the warrant` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company issues a share warrant`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that issues a share warrant"
    ELSE IF `the articles authorise the company to provide for the payment of the future dividends on the shares included in the warrant`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if so authorised by its articles" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F17: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- src:10074 | (4) No share warrant may be issued by a company (irrespective of whether its articles purport to authorise it to do so) on or after the day on which section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 comes into force.
@ref s 779(4) No share warrant may be issued on or after the day on which section 84 of the 2015 Act comes into force (src:10074)
GIVEN `the day on which the share warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(4) the bar on issuing a share warrant applies` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the share warrant is issued` AT LEAST `the day on which section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the bar applies "irrespective of whether its articles purport to authorise it to do so"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or after the day on which section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 comes into force" (a day before it)

-- src:10078 | (1) If in Scotland a person—
-- src:10079 | (a) with intent to defraud, forges or alters, or offers, utters, disposes of, or puts off, knowing the same to be forged or altered, any share warrant or coupon, or any document purporting to be a share warrant or coupon issued in pursuance of this Act, or
-- src:10080 | (b) by means of any such forged or altered share warrant, coupon or document—
-- src:10081 | (i) demands or endeavours to obtain or receive any share or interest in a company under this Act, or
-- src:10082 | (ii) demands or endeavours to receive any dividend or money payment in respect of any such share or interest,
-- src:10083 | knowing the warrant, coupon or document to be forged or altered,
-- src:10084 | he commits an offence.
@ref s 781(1) Offences in connection with share warrants (Scotland): forgery (src:10078-10084)
GIVEN `the person acts in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person forges or alters a share warrant or coupon or a document purporting to be one issued in pursuance of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person offers, utters, disposes of or puts off such a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the document offered, uttered, disposed of or put off to be forged or altered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts by means of such a forged or altered share warrant, coupon or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person demands or endeavours to obtain or receive a share or interest in a company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person demands or endeavours to receive a dividend or money payment in respect of such a share or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the warrant, coupon or document used to be forged or altered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 781(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person acts in Scotland`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in Scotland a person"
    ELSE IF    (    `the person acts with intent to defraud`
                AND (   `the person forges or alters a share warrant or coupon or a document purporting to be one issued in pursuance of this Act`
                     OR (    `the person offers, utters, disposes of or puts off such a document`
                         AND `the person knows the document offered, uttered, disposed of or put off to be forged or altered`)))
            OR (    `the person acts by means of such a forged or altered share warrant, coupon or document`
                AND (   `the person demands or endeavours to obtain or receive a share or interest in a company under this Act`
                     OR `the person demands or endeavours to receive a dividend or money payment in respect of such a share or interest`)
                AND `the person knows the warrant, coupon or document used to be forged or altered`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in Scotland a person (a) with intent to defraud, ... or (b) by means of any such forged or altered share warrant, ... he commits an offence." (the if fails: fork F6)

-- src:10085 | (2) If in Scotland a person without lawful authority or excuse (of which proof lies on him)—
-- src:10086 | (a) engraves or makes on any plate, wood, stone, or other material, any share warrant or coupon purporting to be—
-- src:10087 | (i) a share warrant or coupon issued or made by any particular company in pursuance of this Act, or
-- src:10088 | (ii) a blank share warrant or coupon so issued or made, or
-- src:10089 | (iii) a part of such a share warrant or coupon, or
-- src:10090 | (b) uses any such plate, wood, stone, or other material, for the making or printing of any such share warrant or coupon, or of any such blank share warrant or coupon or of any part of such a share warrant or coupon, or
-- src:10091 | (c) knowingly has in his custody or possession any such plate, wood, stone, or other material,
-- src:10092 | he commits an offence.
@ref s 781(2) Offences in connection with share warrants (Scotland): plates and other material (src:10085-10092)
GIVEN `the person acts in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves lawful authority or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person engraves or makes on a plate, wood, stone or other material a share warrant or coupon purporting to be one issued or made by a particular company in pursuance of this Act, or a blank one, or a part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses such a plate, wood, stone or other material for making or printing such a share warrant or coupon or a part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly has such a plate, wood, stone or other material in custody or possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 781(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person acts in Scotland`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in Scotland a person"
    ELSE IF `the person proves lawful authority or excuse`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful authority or excuse (of which proof lies on him)"
         ELSE IF    `the person engraves or makes on a plate, wood, stone or other material a share warrant or coupon purporting to be one issued or made by a particular company in pursuance of this Act, or a blank one, or a part of one`
                 OR `the person uses such a plate, wood, stone or other material for making or printing such a share warrant or coupon or a part of one`
                 OR `the person knowingly has such a plate, wood, stone or other material in custody or possession`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) engraves or makes ..., (b) uses ..., (c) knowingly has ... he commits an offence." (the if fails: fork F6)

-- src:10093 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable on summary conviction to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale (or both).
@ref s 781(3) liable on summary conviction to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding level 5 (or both) (src:10093)
`s 781(3) the penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE

-- src:10094 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) is liable—
-- src:10095 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years or a fine (or both);
-- src:10096 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 781(4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) is liable (src:10094-10096)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 781(4) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 7, unit IS Years)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` WITH `fraction of the statutory maximum` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) on conviction on indictment, ... (b) on summary conviction"

§§ `Supplementary provisions (s 782)`

-- src:10099 | (1) If a company on which a notice has been served requiring it to make good any default in complying with—
-- src:10100 | (a) section 769(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on allotment),
-- src:10101 | (b) section 776(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer), or
-- src:10102 | (c) section 780(1) (duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on surrender of share warrant),
-- src:10103 | fails to make good the default within ten days after service of the notice, the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to him may apply to the court.
@ref s 782(1) Issue of certificates etc: court order to make good default (src:10099-10103)
DECLARE `s 782(1) the default the notice requires the company to make good` IS ONE OF
    `s 782(1)(a) default in complying with section 769(1)`
    `s 782(1)(b) default in complying with section 776(1)`
    `s 782(1)(c) default in complying with section 780(1)`
    `s 782(1) some other default`

@ref s 782(1) within ten days after service of the notice (src:10099-10103)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 782(1) the last day for making good the default` MEANS
    `the day on which the notice was served on the company` PLUS 10

@ref s 782(1) the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to him may apply to the court (src:10099-10103)
GIVEN `the default the notice requires the company to make good` IS A `s 782(1) the default the notice requires the company to make good`
      `the day on which the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company made good the default` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the applicant is the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 782(1) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the default the notice requires the company to make good`
    WHEN `s 782(1) some other default` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) section 769(1) ..., (b) section 776(1) ..., or (c) section 780(1)"
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `the applicant is the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to them`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to him"
        ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the company made good the default`
             WHEN JUST madeGood THEN
                 IF madeGood GREATER THAN `s 782(1) the last day for making good the default` `the day on which the notice was served on the company`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "fails to make good the default within ten days after service of the notice" (it made good in time: name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F18: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 782(1) the last day for making good the default` `the day on which the notice was served on the company`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within ten days after service of the notice" (the ten days have not yet ended: name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F18, as above)

-- src:10104 | (2) The court may on such an application make an order directing the company and any officer of it to make good the default within such time as may be specified in the order.
@ref s 782(2) The court may on such an application make an order (src:10104)
GIVEN `an application has been made to the court under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 782(2) the court may order the company and any officer of it to make good the default within the time specified in the order` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to the court under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such an application"

-- src:10105 | (3) The order may provide that all costs (in Scotland, expenses) of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the company or by an officer of it responsible for the default.
@ref s 782(3) The order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the company or by an officer (src:10105)
GIVEN `the court has made an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 782(3) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the company or by an officer of it responsible for the default` MEANS
    IF `the court has made an order under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order may provide"
